therClient.get` now retries when the server returns 503, making at most 3 attempts in total. I tried it against a local HTTP server and all four cases behaved as expected.\n\n**How it works** (`weather.py`):\n- If a request gets a 503 and attempts remain, the client waits and tries again. The wait doubles each time: `backoff * 2**attempt`, which with the default is 0.5s, then 1s.\n- If the third attempt also gets a 503, that error is raised to the caller.\n- Other HTTP errors, like a 500, are raised straight away with no retry.\n- Network errors and timeouts are not retried either, since you only asked about 503.\n- There's a new constructor argument, `backoff=0.5` (seconds), so the wait can be changed or set near zero in tests. The attempt limit is the class constant `MAX_ATTEMPTS = 3`.\n\n**Results from the local server** (with `backoff=0.05`):\n\n| Server behaviour | Requests made | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Succeeds first time | 1 | data returned |\n| 503 twice, then success | 3 | data returned (~0.15s) |\n| 503 every time | 3 | `HTTPError 503` raised |\n| 500 | 1 | `HTTPError 500` raised, no retry |\n\nThe repo has no test suite, so this was a one-off check and no test file was added.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 35125, "requests_cache_write": 143505, "requests_cost_usd": 0.7579779999999999, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1669, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial21", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 100, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:51:00.339283+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 22.294, "t_checker_s": 1.916, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinki